From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergio Marin <sergio.marin@pantacor.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:05:03 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rdawlan: keep the shutdown path minimal

.shutdown ran the full teardown on every reboot: unregister the netdev,
detach cfg80211, release an RTNL it might not hold (wland_del_if), with the
bus timers and work items still running, which could hang device_shutdown
so the board never reset. It also left the chip powered and mid-session,
so the next boot started against a busy chip.

Stop the chip's SDIO interrupt and power it off; leave the rest to the
reset.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor driver, not upstream]
---
 .../net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_linux.c  | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_linux.c b/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_linux.c
index e907cda..596bac9 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_linux.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/rdaw80211/rdawlan/wland_linux.c
@@ -1103,15 +1103,24 @@ static void __exit wlanfmac_module_exit(void)
 	WLAND_DBG(DEFAULT, TRACE, "Done\n");
 }
 
+/*
+ * Reboot and power-off path: keep it minimal. It used to run the full
+ * teardown (unregister the netdev, detach cfg80211, take and release an RTNL
+ * it might not hold) with the bus timers and work items still live, which
+ * could hang device_shutdown so the board never reset; and it left the chip
+ * powered and mid-session for the next boot. Now: stop the chip's interrupt
+ * and power it off.
+ */
 void rda_wland_shutdown(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct wland_bus *bus_if = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
-	struct wland_sdio_dev *sdiodev = bus_if->bus_priv.sdio;
+	struct wland_sdio_dev *sdiodev = bus_if ? bus_if->bus_priv.sdio : NULL;
 
 	WLAND_DBG(DEFAULT, TRACE, "Enter\n");
 	cancel_work_sync(&wland_driver_work);
-	wland_sdio_release(sdiodev->bus);
-	wland_debugfs_exit();
+	if (sdiodev && sdiodev->func)
+		wland_sdio_intr_unregister(sdiodev);
+	rda_wifi_power_off();
 	WLAND_DBG(DEFAULT, TRACE, "Done\n");
 }
 
